# Shell hygiene

**No background shells. Stop everything you start before you finish.**

Each **`Shell`** invocation on Windows typically spawns **powershell.exe** (+ **conhost.exe**). On capable workstations, **parallel independent `Shell` calls in one turn are allowed** (e.g. tests + git inspection). Prefer **`Read`**, **`Grep`**, and **`Glob`** over shell for exploration-only work.

## Windows shell (PowerShell only)

Agent shells run **Windows PowerShell**, not bash. Do **not** use Unix-only commands or pipelines such as `head`, `tail`, `sed`, `awk`, `grep`, `find`, `xargs`, or `wc`.

For file preview and search, use **`Read`**, **`Grep`**, and **`Glob`** — not `cat | head` or similar.

When shell file I/O is unavoidable, use PowerShell idioms:

| Need | Use |
|------|-----|
| First N lines | `Get-Content path -TotalCount N` |
| Last N lines | `Get-Content path -Tail N` |
| Search in file | `Select-String pattern path` or **`Grep`** |
| Find files by name | `Get-ChildItem -Recurse -Filter *.ext` or **`Glob`** |

Do not switch to WSL/bash just to run Unix text tools unless the user explicitly requests a Linux shell.

## Hard limits

- **Parallel `Shell` calls are allowed** when commands are independent (owner override 2026-08-08). Do not run dependent steps in parallel (e.g. commit before tests finish).
- Do not background shell commands unless the user explicitly asked for a long-running process.
- **No nested launcher:** invoke repo scripts directly from repo root (e.g. `.\scripts\ci\agent-compile-check.ps1 -ProjectPath …`), not wrapped in `powershell -NoProfile -File …`.
- **No WSL / bash / sh** for routine agent work unless the user explicitly requests a Linux shell command.
- **No speculative shells:** do not run full-solution `dotnet build`, `dotnet test`, `npm`/`pnpm` install, Docker, or broad `git` history unless the user asked or the task cannot complete without it.
- Never start dev servers, watchers, log tails, or `gh pr checks --watch` unless the user requested them.
- Before ending a turn that used shells: stop every process you started and report how many agent shells remain.
- **Task `shell` subagents** are allowed for command-heavy work per **`Agent-Execution-Policy.mdc`**.

## `block_until_ms` tiers (Shell tool)

`block_until_ms` is the **maximum wait before backgrounding**, not idle time after success. Use the **smallest tier that fits**; never default to 600000.

| Tier | `block_until_ms` | Command class | Examples |
|------|------------------|---------------|----------|
| **Fast** | **15000–30000** (default **30000**) | Inspection, git, gh, listing | `git status`, `git diff`, `gh pr view`, `ls`, `pwd`, `Get-ChildItem` |
| **Medium** | **120000–180000** | Scoped build/test/lint | `.\scripts\ci\agent-compile-check.ps1`, `dotnet build *.slnf`, single test project, `npm run lint` |
| **Slow** | **300000–600000** | Full solution or heavy I/O | full `dotnet build`, full `dotnet test`, `npm ci`, Docker pull |

**Never** use **600000** for git, gh, or read-only inspection. If a fast command exceeds 30s, suspect a **hung shell** (see cleanup below), not a need for a longer ceiling.

## Git

When git inspection is needed, **`git status`**, **`git diff`**, and **`git log`** may run in **parallel** with other independent shells, or **chained** in one call when only git is needed:

```powershell
git status --short; git diff --stat; git log -5 --oneline
```

## Terminal heartbeat

For commands expected **>15s** (Medium/Slow tiers), emit **`STILL EXECUTING... HH:mm:ss`** every **8 seconds** while the child runs. See **`shell-heartbeat.mdc`** for the wrapper pattern and skip rules.

## Compile verification

- Run **at most one** scoped compile check per task (plus **one** retry on exit code **1** on the **same** scope).
- Skip compile when the user defers verification or the turn was read-only / docs-only.
- Use: `.\scripts\ci\agent-compile-check.ps1` with `-ProjectPath` or `-Ui`.

## Cleanup script

When orphaned agent shells accumulate or commands feel stuck:

```powershell
.\scripts\cleanup-agent-shells.ps1 -DryRun   # preview
.\scripts\cleanup-agent-shells.ps1 -Force    # stop matches
```

The script targets Cursor agent one-shot `powershell -c` wrappers and script runners. It skips integrated IDE terminal tabs (`-noexit`).

## User overrides

If the user says **no shell**, **read-only**, or **single-thread / at most one command per turn**, treat that as stricter than this rule for the rest of the session.
